  "response_complete": true,
  "response_text": "If you have unprotected sex, you should watch for the following warning signs of possible sexually transmitted infections (STIs) after the sexual encounter:\n\n  1. Unusual discharge from the vagina or penis\n  2. Pain or burning during urination or sexual intercourse\n  3. Painful or swollen testicles or vagina\n  4. Unusual bleeding or spotting between periods\n  5. Unusual itching or irritation in the genital area\n  6. Unusual fatigue or weakness\n  7. Unusual changes in sexual desire or pleasure\n\nIf you experience any of these warning signs, it is important to seek medical attention as soon as possible. It is also important to get tested for STIs if you have had unprotected sex, even if you do not have any symptoms. This is because some STIs can be asymptomatic, meaning they do not cause any noticeable symptoms, but can still be transmitted to others. It is also important to use condoms consistently and correctly to reduce the risk of STIs.",
